            <ArticleTitle>Arthroscopic Excision of an Intraarticular Osteoid Osteoma in the Distal Femur.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>475-480</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An intraarticular osteoid osteoma of the knee is uncommon, and its treatment is challenging. The authors present a case of arthroscopic excision of an intraarticular osteoid osteoma in the distal femur, which was accessible through the knee joint. After confirming the nidus of the osteoid osteoma by computed tomography, the lesion was completely removed arthroscopically. The patient reported complete pain relief immediately after surgery. This case demonstrates that intraarticular osteoid osteomas in the knee joint can be treated by arthroscopic excision and that good results can be obtained.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
